Introduce a refactor to complete the first end-to-end assignment publishing pipeline while keeping runtime behavior stable except for activation of the leader role via existing watcher/reconcile logic resulting from a user request to endpoint GET /make-leader.

1. Introduce Global Configuration Package
* Create a new config package under src/config.
* It must contain a single globally accessible NodeID value.
* NodeID must be initialized exactly once from os.Getenv("NODE_ID") in main().
* After initialization, NodeID must be read-only and accessed across the application via a getter function config.NodeID().
* This package must have no internal dependencies to prevent circular imports.

2. Update Assignment Model
* Modify src/models/models.go to update the Assignment struct. It must include fields matching the following structural needs:
  * NodeID (string, JSON tag "node_id")
  * ID (string, JSON tag "id")
  * Role (string, JSON tag "role")
  * Config (json.RawMessage, JSON tag "config")

3. Refactor Network Abstractions
* Replace the existing NodeController abstraction in src/infra/server.go.
* Remove the CampaignForLeadership method entirely from all interfaces and implementations.
* Introduce a new interface named AssignmentCreator with a single method:
  CreateAssignment(ctx context.Context, assignment models.Assignment) error
* The HTTP server must depend exclusively on AssignmentCreator.

4. Update the HTTP Handler
* Update the /make-leader handler in src/infra/server.go to explicitly enforce an HTTP GET request.
* The handler must construct a models.Assignment object containing:
  * NodeID set to config.NodeID()
  * ID set to the string "initial"
  * Role set to the string "leader"
  * Config left as an empty JSON object
* The handler must call CreateAssignment with this object.
* The handler must respond immediately with HTTP 200 and log an entry indicating a leader assignment request was submitted.

5. Implement Persistence Layer
* Modify src/adapters/etcd-store.go to implement the AssignmentCreator interface on Store.
* Implement CreateAssignment(ctx, assignment) error to perform an etcd transaction:
  1. Serialize and store the full assignment struct as JSON under: assignments/definitions/<assignment.ID>
  2. Store the assignment ID in a JSON array under: assignments/nodes/<assignment.NodeID>. IDs are added to the array by reading it, adding to it and then writing the new array to the Store.
* The node assignment list must be overwritten with a single-element array containing only the new assignment ID.
* Ensure proper error handling and return wrapped errors if etcd operations fail.

6. Refactor Runtime Execution Engine & Registry Signatures
* Modify src/roles/registry.go to update the RoleFunc definition. Every registered role function must now accept the complete assignment struct:
  type RoleFunc func(ctx context.Context, asg *models.Assignment) error
* Update src/roles/runtime.go so that the execution pipeline passes r.Definition directly into the registry logic handler: entry.Logic(ctx, r.Definition).
* Modify src/roles/leader.go to match this signature. Inside RunLeaderRole, log an activation message using fields parsed directly from the passed assignment parameter: Node <asg.NodeID> is now acting as cluster leader for assignment <asg.ID>.
* The leader role remains passive after initialization and does not call etcd or AssignmentCreator.

7. Wire Application Baseline
* Modify src/main.go to initialize the global config package exactly once at startup from os.Getenv("NODE_ID").
* Immediately following initialization, src/main.go must become a regular consumer of config.NodeID() like all other application packages. Remove localized nodeID string tracking variables.
* Pass config.NodeID() where needed to wire the new interface into the HTTP server constructor, initialization routines, and engine components.
* The existing watcher/reconciliation pipeline logic must remain structurally unchanged. It must continue to watch assignments/nodes/<nodeID>, fetch definitions via etcd, map them to functions using the registry, and start AssignmentRuntime.

8. Verification Pipeline
Ensure that after the refactor, execution flows cleanly along this end-to-end pipeline:
1. GET /make-leader triggers assignment creation.
2. etcd stores assignment definition and node mapping.
3. Watcher in main.go detects the state mutation.
4. Reconciler matches definitions and starts the runtime.
5. Leader role logs its activation message dynamically using the parameters passed to it by the registry runner.
